UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105028863723&doi=10.1109%2fEIT67313.2025.11232424&partnerID=40&md5=686f1e4ac59f0551e35da0a55fbf334d
AD  - Taiyuan University of Technology, College of Computer Science and Technology, China
AB  - In the realm of edge computing and mobile devices, deploying efficient image classification models is crucial due to limited computational resources. This paper proposes a lightweight CNN based on MobileNetV2, optimized through knowledge distillation and structured pruning techniques. By leveraging a pre-trained ResNet50 as the teacher model, knowledge distillation transfers essential features to the student MobileNetV2, enhancing its performance while maintaining a compact size. Subsequently, L1-norm based pruning reduces redundant parameters by up to 50%, significantly lowering model complexity without substantial accuracy degradation. Evaluations on the CIFAR-10 dataset demonstrate that the baseline MobileNet achieves 95.2% accuracy with 3.54M parameters, while the improved model attains 94.1% accuracy with only 1.77M parameters, halving inference time and memory usage. These results highlight the model's suitability for resource-constrained environments, offering a balanced trade-off between efficiency and accuracy. Extensive ablation studies confirm the contributions of each component, paving the way for practical deployments in real-world applications.  © 2025 IEEE.
