AB  - Aiming at the challenges of small litchi gall target detection being susceptible to complex background interference and the difficulty of balancing accuracy and efficiency in existing lightweight models, this study proposes a lightweight detection model named FDE-YOLO with YOLOv8n as the baseline. Litchi gall images were collected from Huizhou, Guangdong Province to construct a comprehensive dataset, followed by systematic preprocessing and augmentation. To optimize the model performance, the original backbone network was replaced with FasterNet to reduce computational overhead, a C2f_D module was designed to enhance multi-scale feature fusion, and an Efficient Multi-Scale Attention (EMAttention) mechanism was integrated into the detection head to strengthen small target features and suppress background noise. Experimental results demonstrate that FDE-YOLO achieves a mean average precision at 0.5 intersection over union (mAP0.5) of 83.5% and a mean average precision at 0.5 to 0.95 intersection over union (mAP0.5:0.95) of 51.6% with only 1.85 million parameters. Compared with mainstream lightweight models, FDE-YOLO not only exhibits superior detection accuracy but also significantly reduces computational complexity and model size. Moreover, it demonstrates stronger robustness under complex scenarios such as illumination variations and Gaussian blur. This model realizes the dual improvement of detection accuracy and lightweight performance, providing a feasible machine vision solution for the rapid and accurate detection of litchi galls in practical agricultural applications.  © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
