AB  - Mask R-CNN, has been widely applied to many areas in the last decade due to its outstanding performance regarding instance segmentation. The algorithm has various performances under different situations. So, some methods are required to reinforce its performance. This work focused on its performance with noised images. The model was trained with the images containing any annotations of cars in the Coco2017 dataset and evaluated with the images with and without noises. Besides, a Denoising AutoEncoder (DAE) is trained and used to eliminate the noise in the images. The trained DAE has a loss lower than 0.2 based on the metric called Mean Square Error (MSE) between the noise-free and reconstructed images. After the training the Mask R-CNN model, it can reach an Average Precision (AP) at 35.22 and 32.41, respectively for bounding box and segmentation. The AP drops significantly to lower than one-third as before with the noised images. Despite that the DAE recovers the images from noise, the prediction results are still not acceptable. That might be caused by the entropy loss when the images are processed by the DAE.  © 2022 IEEE.
