AB  - Crop damage from rhesus macaques presents significant challenge in Nepal's mid-hill regions, with reported losses reaching 45% of agricultural yields. This paper introduces EdgeYOLO, an AI-IoT system that combines YOLOv8n with Raspberry Pi 5 hardware and USB camera input for real-Time monkey detection and farmer alerting via Slack notifications. Our methodology encompasses dataset collection and augmentation, model training, NCNN conversion with quantization, runtime debouncing, and field trials. Experimental results demonstrate that the system achieves 91.7% mAP@0.5 on test data and 88% accuracy in field conditions, operating at 15-22 FPS depending on optimization settings. When benchmarked against YOLOv5n (TensorFlow Lite) and MobileNet-SSD (OpenVINO), EdgeYOLO exhibits superior speed-Accuracy trade-offs. We discuss current limitations and propose future enhancements including sensor fusion and multi-node coordination.  © 2026 IEEE.
