AB  - Restoring a high-quality image and removing noise from it has become crucial for processing images further for tasks like object segmentation, tracking, and detection. In this study, we employ a convolutional neural network (CNN) model for deep learning to achieve image denoising. Initially, the images are subjected to Gaussian white noise levels ranging from 1% to 10%. The CNN model is then applied to denoise the images. The denoised images are subsequently analyzed through both quantitative and qualitative methods. Qualitative analysis evaluates factors such as object structure, uniform and non-uniform regions, texture, smoothness, and edge preservation. For quantitative analysis, we use metrics like peak signal-to-noise ratio (PSNR) and structural similarity index measurement (SSIM). The results from our experiments indicate that the CNN model effectively removes a substantial amount of Gaussian noise and successfully restores the image quality.  © 2026 Author(s).
