AD  - Taiyuan University of Technology, Software Engineering, Taiyuan, China
AB  - Aiming at the problem of low precision in plant disease detection within complex backgrounds, this paper proposes an improved YOLOv8n-based method. Based on the original YOLOv8n model, Multi-Head Attention mechanism is introduced at the final stage of the backbone network to enhance semantic representation of deep features. In the neck, the original FPN is exchanged by BiFPN to achieve more efficient bidirectional feature fusion. In the detection head, the original head is replaced by an ASFF head to further achieve adaptive fusion of cross-scale features based on the BiFPN output. Comparative results reveal that, versus original YOLOv8n model, a proposed method improves mAP@0.5:0.95 by 10.4%, mAP@0.5 by 12.1%, and recall by 35.9%. This fully demonstrates that the method is more accurate than the original YOLOv8n model.  © COPYRIGHT SPIE. Downloading of the abstract is permitted for personal use only.
