TI  - Automatic Weed Identification in Lawn Management Based on Viewpoint-Aware Data Augmentation and YOLOv12n-seg Instance Segmentation
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings - 2025 17th International Conference on Signal Processing Systems, ICSPS 2025
SP  - 917
EP  - 921
DO  - 10.1109/ICSPS66615.2025.11347625
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105034712077&doi=10.1109%2fICSPS66615.2025.11347625&partnerID=40&md5=32b511b24ddece41acc583c105e63eb2
AD  - Graduate Institute of Intelligent Manufacturing Technology, National Taiwan University of Science and Technology Taipei, Taiwan
AD  - National Taiwan University of Science and Technology Taipei, Department of Information Management, Taiwan
AB  - Weed detection in intelligent lawn management often relies on top-view images, which inadequately reflect complex real-world robotic perspectives. This study addresses this domain gap by proposing a viewpoint aware weed detection pipeline using YOLO (You Only Look Once) based instance segmentation models. Three YOLO architectures (YOLOv8n-seg, YOLOv11n-seg, YOLOv12n-seg) were trained on a custom GBIF (Global Biodiversity Information Facility) dataset, augmented with rotation, perspective transformations, and real-world topview and front-view images from the NTUST (National Taiwan University of Science and Technology) campus. Models were evaluated across augmented dataset variants and distinct test sets (GBIF, top-view, front-view) using Precision, Recall, mAP@0.5, and mAP@0.5:0.95 for both bounding boxes and segmentation masks. Results demonstrate that data augmentation, particularly viewpoint-aware transformations and real image inclusion, significantly improves generalization to challenging viewpoints. YOLOv11n-seg achieved the highest overall performance, especially in segmentation accuracy. Notably, YOLOv12n-seg, trained from scratch, showed the greatest performance gain, matching or surpassing pretrained models on the most augmented dataset. This research confirms that combining geometric augmentation with realistic, perspective-aligned data effectively bridges the gap between ideal training conditions and real-world robotic deployment, offering valuable insights for autonomous weeding and mobile agricultural robotics. © 2025 IEEE.
