AD  - College of Information Engineering, Northwest A&F University, Shaanxi, Yangling, 712100, China
AD  - Shenzhen Agricultural Science and Technology Promotion Center, Guangdong, Nanshan, 518000, China
AB  - Deep learning-based instance segmentation constitutes a critical prerequisite for precision agriculture, enabling accurate variety classification and individual plant localization that underpin subsequent phenotypic trait extraction. However, existing lightweight models suffer from feature loss when handling leafy vegetables with subtle textures and high phenotypic similarity, leading to classification confusion and blurred boundaries that compromise trait measurement accuracy. To address this, we propose a lightweight multi-growth-stage instance segmentation framework, named Lightweight VegetableMask (LVegMask). Specifically, we construct a multi-view multi-stage Leaf Vegetable Segmentation (LVS) dataset covering various varieties and growth stages. We then design a light backbone Mobile Coordinate Attention Network (MobileCANet) by integrating Mobile Convolutional Neural Network (MobileNet) with Coordinate Attention to reduce parameter counts. Furthermore, A global Enhancement and Path Aggregation Feature Pyramid Networks (EPA-FPN) architecture is proposed to enhance multi-scale feature fusion. At last, Patch Discrete Cosine Transform (PatchDCT) module and Boundary Loss function are introduced to achieve significant improvement in boundary accuracy. Experimental results on the LVS dataset demonstrate that LVegMask achieves a mean Average Precision (mAP) of 92.9% with 34.1 Million (M) parameters and 91.8 Giga Floating-point Operations (GFLOPs), while maintaining an inference speed of 35.6 Frames Per Second (FPS). Validation on an Orange Pi embedded board demonstrates the model’s feasibility for edge deployment. These results indicate that LVegMask effectively balances accuracy and efficiency, facilitating the deployment of instance segmentation technology in resource-constrained agricultural environments. The dataset is available at https://www.modelscope.cn/datasets/OrchidX/LVS . © 2026 Elsevier Ltd.
