AB  - This paper presents EffiRepYOLO, a novel lightweight model optimized for real-time commodity recognition in resource-constrained environments. By integrating EfficientNetV2 and RepVit into the YOLOv8 framework, the proposed model achieves a superior balance between accuracy and computational efficiency. The redesigned backbone replaces CSPDarknet53 with EfficientNetV2's FusedMBConv, and MBConv modules, reducing parameters by 15% while maintaining feature extraction capability. Additionally, RepVit's reparameterized multi-head self-attention mechanism enhances global contextual understanding in the Neck section. Evaluated on the MS COCO dataset, EffiRepYOLO achieves 75.1% mAP @ 0.5 and 54.3% mAP@0.5:0.95 with only 2.7M parameters and 8.2G FLOPs, outperforming existing lightweight models like YOLOv7-tiny and YOLOv8 variants. The proposed model provides a practical solution for deploying high-accuracy commodity recognition systems on resource-constrained edge devices. © 2025 IEEE.
