AD  - School of Big Data and Computer Science, Guangdong Baiyun University, Guangdong, Guangzhou, China
AB  - To address the severe disease missed detection problem in deep learning models such as You Only Look Once version 8 (YOLOv8) caused by background interference-including water surface reflections, leaf occlusion, and weed shadows-in complex paddy field environments, this paper proposes YOLOv8-EP (Efficient Multi-scale Attention and P2 detection head). Building on the YOLOv8-small (YOLOv8s) baseline, the model introduces an Efficient Multi-Scale Attention (EMA) mechanism to suppress complex background interference and a P2 multi-scale detection head to capture fine-grained disease lesions. These two components work synergistically across both the feature space and network structure dimensions to reduce the missed detection rate. On a dataset of 4,380 images covering four rice disease categories, YOLOv8-EP achieves a mean Average Precision (mAP@0.5) of 67.7% and a Recall of 68.2%, representing improvements of 3.2 percentage points and 2.6 percentage points over the YOLOv8s baseline, respectively, with a 6.9% improvement in mAP@0.5:0.95. Ablation experiments confirm a positive synergistic gain between EMA and P2. This work provides a novel lightweight architectural paradigm for precision agriculture, demonstrating that coupling structural multi-scale expansion with parallel semantic purification can significantly advance the deployment of real-Time edge-AI infrastructure in unconstrained, open-world agricultural environments.  © 2026 IEEE.
